The United States copy of the IPK is maintained by, you guessed it, NIST.

533
00:35:48,981 --> 00:35:55,980
The International Prototype Kilogram is a platinum meridium artifact that looks just like this one right here under this bell jar.

534
00:35:55,981 --> 00:36:04,980
At the time when the kilogram was manufactured and sanctioned, 40 replicas were made and distributed to the signatories of the meter convention.

